schema: "0.4"
id: fim-notebook-livebook-and-widgets-kino-plotly-02-dense-reactive-stress-widget
type: visualization
quality: high
solution: kino-plotly
category: notebook-livebook-and-widgets
variant: dense-reactive-stress-widget
prompt:
  system: |-
    You are a senior Elixir Livebook scientific visualization engineer. Output only one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell for Kino.Plotly. No Markdown fences, no prose outside code. Prioritize bounded high-density figures and responsive notebook behavior.
  text: |-
    Create a dense reactive Kino.Plotly stress visualization. Generate deterministic bounded data for multiple Plotly traces, such as a heatmap plus contour, scatter3d point cloud, surface plus projected contour, or multi-series line chart. Validate trace array lengths or z matrix dimensions, downsample or aggregate before rendering, and include layout controls such as legend orientation, hovermode, scene camera, margins, and colorscales.

    Requirements: document Livebook compatibility, Plotly trace data shape, matrix orientation, and browser-rendering limits; include fallback smaller data and wrapper fallback notes; include accessible labels, hover text, color scale legends, and non-color encodings; include safe execution checks for huge traces, remote data, credentials, eval, shell calls, and unavailable Kino.Plotly wrapper.
  provider_options:
    max_tokens: 8192
    temperature: 0.2
    top_p: 0.9
output:
  text_format: elixir
  artifact_kind: livebook-kino-plotly-stress-cell
  formats:
  - format: exs
evaluation:
  checklist:
  - "Import check: generated code installs kino_plotly and kino, creates multiple bounded traces, and calls Kino.Plotly.new/2."
  - "Notebook compatibility: comments identify Livebook/Kino, Plotly.js browser limits, and wrapper availability."
  - "Reactive state: figure rebuild or rerun state is explicit; optional updates are bounded and do not rely on uncontrolled browser loops."
  - "Data shape: trace arrays, z matrix rows/columns, lengths, colorscale fields, and layout domains are validated or documented."
  - "Accessibility and fallback: hover text, labels, legends, fallback smaller data, and readable color scales are present."
  - "Safe execution: no huge unbounded traces, remote data, credentials, eval, shell commands, or unguarded wrapper assumptions."
  rubric:
  - name: Format validity
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Output is one complete ASCII Elixir Livebook code cell with no Markdown fences or explanatory wrapper."
    - "The code is valid and all traces are in a list passed to Kino.Plotly.new/2."
    - "Layout uses correct Plotly fields for 2D and 3D charts."
  - name: Semantic completeness
    weight: 30
    criteria:
    - "Implements a dense Plotly stress chart with multiple traces, validation, downsampling, and layout tuning."
    - "Uses Plotly-specific trace type strings, colorscales, hover, legend, and scene options."
    - "Includes notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - name: UX/structural quality
    weight: 25
    criteria:
    - "Dense visualization remains legible through sampling, legends, colorscales, and hover text."
    - "Layout choices avoid clipped labels and ambiguous axes."
    - "Fallback and performance notes are visible in comments or status output."
  - name: Robustness
    weight: 15
    criteria:
    - "Handles empty data, matrix transposition, mismatched lengths, outliers, and missing wrapper dependency."
    - "Keeps generated data deterministic and bounded."
    - "Documents when to switch to the Kino.JS fallback or downsample further."
  pass_conditions:
  - "All required YAML fields are present and the generated artifact is one valid ASCII Elixir Livebook cell."
  - "Rubric weights are exactly Format validity 30, Semantic completeness 30, UX/structural quality 25, Robustness 15."
  - "The prompt requires notebook/livebook compatibility, reactive state, data shape, accessibility, fallback, and safe execution checks."
  - "The solution remains Kino.Plotly-centered and treats browser rendering limits explicitly."
tags:
- fim
- notebook-livebook-and-widgets
- livebook
- kino-plotly
- dense-reactive-stress-widget

